# Eleva Icons (`@eleva/icons`)

## Hard rules

1. Import icon components from `@eleva/icons` (SSR-safe). Import `NavIcon` / `ElevaIcon` from `@eleva/icons/client` only in client files.
2. **Never** import `@phosphor-icons/react` or `lucide-react` outside `packages/icons`.
3. **Server layouts**: sidebar nav uses `NavIconName` string literals (e.g. `"UserIcon"`), never Phosphor components — functions cannot cross the RSC boundary. Client `NavMenuItemLink` resolves via `getNavIcon` from `@eleva/icons/client`.
4. Named imports only — do not re-export the full Phosphor catalog from app code.
5. New icon? Add to `packages/icons/src/icons.tsx`, then consume from `@eleva/icons`.

## Weights

| Context | Weight | Size |
|---------|--------|------|
| Sidebar (idle) | `light` | 20px |
| Sidebar (hover/focus) | `regular` | 20px + subtle scale |
| Sidebar (active) | `duotone` | 20px + left accent bar |
| Reduced motion (active) | `fill` | no scale / no duotone morph |
| UI chrome | `regular` | 16px |
| Illustrations | `duotone` | ≥ 32px |

## Duotone brand colors

- Primary: `text-eleva-primary` or `text-sidebar-primary`
- Secondary layer: `duotoneColor="rgb(var(--eleva-primary-light))"` via `ElevaIcon` / `NavIcon`

## shadcn

[`packages/ui/components.json`](../../packages/ui/components.json) uses `"iconLibrary": "phosphor"`. Regenerate UI primitives with the CLI when adding shadcn components.
